Important
    - Num("3.45 iu3r") automatically creates a new unit in the dynamic file as "iu3x
      !base!".  This is dangerous, as it could have been a typo, but then that unit will
      exist until the user deletes it.  The default units behavior is 'iu3r\n' will
      return "Unknown unit 'iu3r'"
        - Num.base() should be the only way to register a new unit, as it calls
